<title>CROATIA: Croatia wants more welfare spending next year.</title>
<headline>Croatia wants more welfare spending next year.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatian government has drafted a new law on social welfare, foreseeing higher expenditures next year, state news agency HINA reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The law, which has yet to be endorsed by parliament, envisages social spending of up to 10 billion kuna against this year's 4.6 billion, the agency said. No further details were given.</p>
<p>Croatia's austerity programme launched in 1993 has efectively curbed inflation, but it also increased poverty.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
